    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d748">

                <pb facs="1021" n="1007" sameAs="frus:frus1944v06/pg1007"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5034 Registration/12–1444: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Appointed Ambassador in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hurley</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Chungking</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-12-14T08:00:00+07:00">December 14,
                            1944—8 a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 9:35 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2017. Final date for registration of foreign companies extended to June 30, 1945
                    (ReEmbs 1959, December 6, 10 a.m.<anchor n="44" xml:id="d748-f1"/>). In letter
                    of December 11 advising Embassy of extension, Economic Affairs Minister requests
                    foreign business concerns be directed to make effective preparations for
                    fulfillment of registration procedure at early date.</p>
                <p>Embassy requests transmission of memoranda from Councils (ReDepts 1494, November
                    16) be expedited.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hurley</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
